# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Verafye — Required Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env.local before running locally or deploying.
# BOTH variables below are REQUIRED. Build will fail at runtime if either is
# missing — there are no silent fallbacks.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Request Demo endpoint — used by:
#   - app/request-demo/RequestDemoClient.js   (Request Demo form)
#   - app/become-a-partner/BecomeAPartnerClient.js  (Partner Enquiry form)
# The path may differ from LEAD_CAPTURE — confirm with backend team.
# Production:
NEXT_PUBLIC_VERAFYE_REQUEST_DEMO_ENDPOINT=https://dashboard.verafye.com/api/external-email/send
# Staging / dev (override as needed):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VERAFYE_REQUEST_DEMO_ENDPOINT=https://dashboard.verafye.dev/api/external-email/send

# Lead capture endpoint — used by:
#   - app/resources/PdfDownloadModal.js   (gated PDF download form)
# This may point to the same API route as REQUEST_DEMO or a distinct one.
# Production:
NEXT_PUBLIC_VERAFYE_LEAD_CAPTURE_ENDPOINT=https://dashboard.verafye.com/api/lead-capture
# Staging / dev (override as needed):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VERAFYE_LEAD_CAPTURE_ENDPOINT=https://dashboard.verafye.dev/api/lead-capture

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# IMPORTANT: NEXT_PUBLIC_ variables are baked into the static JS bundle at
# build time. A missing variable is not detectable at runtime after deployment.
# Always run `npm run build:prod` (which sets both vars) for production builds.
# Never rely on .env.local for production deployments — set vars in your
# hosting provider's environment settings instead.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
